      "text_raw": "In this realization a current\nis generated which is trian-\ngular with its maximum at\n0.5 V, and which becomes\nzero for inputs below 0.2 V\nor higher than 0.8 V.\nThe actual input voltage\nand the Gate voltages are\nplotted versus average input\nvoltage. It is clearly seen\nthat for input voltages larger\nthan 0.5 V, the nMOST\nalready conducts. Also, the\npMOST conducts for input\nvoltages up to 0.5 V. A rail-\nto-rail input range is now\nobtained.",
      "text": "In this realization a current is generated which is triangular with its maximum at 0.5 V, and which becomes zero for inputs below 0.2 V or higher than 0.8 V. The actual input voltage and the Gate voltages are plotted versus average input voltage. It is clearly seen that for input voltages larger than 0.5 V, the nMOST already conducts. Also, the pMOST conducts for input voltages up to 0.5 V. A railto-rail input range is now obtained."
